    "specPath": "specs/043-sidecar-ready-deadline/spec.md",
    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "Amends 013 so the supervisor's ready deadline measures the producer's own startup, not the operating system's assessment of a newly placed executable. A bounded start deadline covers the time from spawn until the producer's code is observed running; the existing ready deadline runs from that observation. Closes the residual 013 records for a ready-timeout under syspolicyd load, and measures the same route on Linux.\n",
    "title": "The witness sidecar's ready deadline starts when its process starts"
